# ---------- Documents, avatar and downloads (Slice E) ----------
# Binaries live behind IFileStorage (local disk, Storage section in appsettings).
# Only the relative path is ever persisted or returned; the media type is derived
# from the file's extension. Every download miss answers the same 404, so the route
# never confirms which document ids exist. requests/avatar-sample.png is a 1x1 PNG
# shipped for the upload below.

### Replace my avatar (multipart, self-only -> { photoUrl })
PUT {{ReviveHRSystem.Web_HostAddress}}/api/employees/1/photo
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data

form-data;
file;requests/avatar-sample.png;image/png

###

### Fetch the avatar my profile now points at
GET {{ReviveHRSystem.Web_HostAddress}}/api/employees/1/photo
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

###

### HR-published official documents (disjoint from the employee vault)
GET {{ReviveHRSystem.Web_HostAddress}}/api/employees/1/hr-documents
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

###

### Download an employee-uploaded document (binary stream; 404 if none is stored)
GET {{ReviveHRSystem.Web_HostAddress}}/api/employees/1/documents/0/download
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

###

### Download an HR-published document (only reachable through the HR route)
GET {{ReviveHRSystem.Web_HostAddress}}/api/employees/1/hr-documents/0/download
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
